---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout title="About Calculator Street — Free Construction Calculators" description="About Calculator Street: US-focused, fast & private calculators for construction. Static, no tracking, built for homeowners & contractors.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] pt-6">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">About Calculator Street</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body [text-wrap:pretty]">Calculator Street (CalculatorSt.com) is a complete construction and home-improvement calculator platform — focused, accurate and private. We cover concrete, gravel, rebar, masonry, roofing, flooring, framing, decking, fencing, landscaping, asphalt and more. Every calculator is hand-verified for US customary and metric units, with clear formulas, worked examples and waste-aware estimates.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Founded 2026 by <span class="font-medium text-ink">Vipul Otari</span> — civil DIY enthusiast focused on US customary units, material densities and waste-aware estimating. Every calculation is verified against supplier scale-house densities and public specs (TxDOT compaction, CPSC playground). Last updated: <span class="font-mono text-xs">2026-08-28</span>.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas flex gap-4 items-start">
        <span class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink text-white dark:bg-white dark:text-black" aria-hidden="true">VO</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">Vipul Otari — Author & Reviewer</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Built and reviewed every calculator. No AI filler — formulas, example tables and assumptions are hand-written and checked against manufacturer yields (e.g., 80-lb concrete = 0.60 ft³). Contact for corrections: <a href="mailto:hello@calculatorst.com" class="text-link underline">hello@calculatorst.com</a> (backup: vipulotari1718@gmail.com). See <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline">Contact</a> for partnerships.</p>
          <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-mute">E-E-A-T: Experience in DIY builds · Expertise verified vs TxDOT/CPSC · Authoritative sources cited per page · Trust via 100% in-browser, no data leaving device.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
        <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Our principles</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-body">
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Static & private</span> — all calculations run in your browser. No database, no accounts, no tracking. <a href="/privacy/" class="text-link underline">Privacy</a> & <a href="/disclaimer/" class="text-link underline">Disclaimer</a> explain limits.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">US-focused</span> — feet, inches, yards, tons, plus metric where useful. Short tons (2000 lb); metric tonnes ×0.907.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Mobile-first</span> — large inputs, thumb-friendly, works on the job site at 320px. No horizontal scroll.</li>
          <li><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Transparent</span> — every page shows formulas, examples, assumptions and related calculators. Cite sources: <a href="https://www.txdot.gov/manuals/brg/offpeo5.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link underline">TxDOT</a> compaction, <a href="https://www.cpsc.gov/safety-education/safety-guides/playgrounds" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link underline">CPSC</a> playground.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">How we verify</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-body"> densities: pea 1.35, crushed 1.40, limestone 1.60 tons/yd³ verified vs scale house averages; concrete bag yields per manufacturer; roof multiplier √(pitch²+144)/12. Waste recommendations from field practice: 10% rectangle, 15% curves/hips.</p>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">Library</h3>
        <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-body">The platform now includes a complete library of construction and home-improvement calculators — organized into sixteen focused categories and searchable from any page. Every calculator is a standalone, indexable tool with its own formula, example, diagram and related tools.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Questions? <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">Contact us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
